# Edge vhost for morrowind.virtastic.app — deployed into the SHARED Caddy's
# /etc/caddy/sites-extra/ (synced to /opt/nostalgia/caddy/sites-extra/morrowind.caddy by CI).
# The shared edge terminates TLS (Cloudflare origin cert) and reverse-proxies to the morrowind
# container by name on the `nostalgia` network.
morrowind.virtastic.app {
	tls /certs/virtastic-origin.crt /certs/virtastic-origin.key

	# Shared security-header snippet from the Nostalgia base Caddyfile.
	# IMPORTANT: verify `sec_headers` does NOT set Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy / -Embedder-Policy.
	# The container already sets COOP=same-origin / COEP=require-corp and they pass through this
	# reverse_proxy; a conflicting/duplicate value from sec_headers would break crossOriginIsolated
	# and the app would show "Browser not supported". If sec_headers sets them, drop them there for
	# this host (or set the three isolation headers here explicitly instead).
	import sec_headers

	# Transparent proxy. Deliberately NO `encode` here: the container serves precompressed .br with
	# Content-Encoding: br, and it must reach the browser un-re-encoded; `encode` would double-encode
	# the wasm and interfere with Range. Cloudflare caches the already-br-encoded response.
	reverse_proxy morrowind:8080
}
